# Quanta repo: ignore EVERYTHING unless explicitly allowed.
#
# Only these are tracked on the remote:
#   README.md   - project readme (root only)
#   .gitignore  - this file
#   compiler/   - the Quanta self-hosting source + promoted binaries
#   docs/       - documentation
#   lib/        - standard library source

# Everything else is internal/local and must NOT be pushed:
#   systems/ agents/ bootstrap/ tools/ scripts/ bin/ src/
#   .hyperresearch/ .claude/ scratch/ temp/ and all junk.
#
# test_suites/, tools/ and .github/ ARE pushed: the CI gate reads
# test_suites/codes/, EXPECTED*.tsv and test_suites/scripts/, so they are
# un-ignored explicitly below. Listing test_suites/ among the ignored names here
# is what caused the original trap.

/*

# The `/*` catch-all above ignores every top-level entry, and gitignore will not
# re-include a file whose PARENT directory is ignored. So `!/test_suites/...` rules
# can rescue nothing: the directory itself stays excluded and every NEW file under
# it is silently dropped. That is the trap this file fell into -- the existing gate
# scripts are tracked (gitignore only applies to untracked files), so test_suites/
# looked correct while 8,864 test sources and every new gate script vanished from
# `git status` and from CI.
#
# Correct shape: un-ignore the DIRECTORY, then blanket-ignore its contents with
# `test_suites/*`, then re-include only what CI actually reads. Inside a
# re-included tree, later exclusions do win, so generated output stays out.
!/test_suites/
# Un-ignore the two directories CI reads. No blanket `test_suites/*` here: it
# would also exclude the 18k test sources and the gate scripts, and gitignore
# will not re-include anything inside a directory the rule already excluded.
!/test_suites/codes/
!/test_suites/scripts/
!/test_suites/EXPECTED.tsv
!/test_suites/EXPECTED_STDLIB.tsv
!/test_suites/EXTERN_EXPECTED.tsv
!/test_suites/numeric_harness.py
# Generated output. LAST match wins, so these beat the re-includes above:
# 89MB of compiled test binaries in bin/, and the scratch files that are not
# tests -- ad-hoc probes, debug scratch, and std_* experiment fragments. Every
# real test follows the *_test.quanta convention and IS tracked; note that most
# tracked tests are deliberately absent from EXPECTED*.tsv (only a subset runs
# in the gate), so "unlisted" is not a reason to leave a test out of git.
test_suites/bin/
# Scratch probes. The leading-underscore form only: a mid-name "probe" also
# occurs in real tests (e.g. std_aerospace_deep_space_probe_const_test.quanta).
test_suites/codes/_*probe*.quanta
test_suites/codes/*probe_scratch*.quanta
test_suites/codes/*_debug.quanta
test_suites/codes/_*.quanta
# NB: do NOT ignore std_*.quanta. There are 9,290 of them and they are real
# tests (std_accounting_benefits_*_const_test.quanta etc). An earlier draft of
# this file excluded them as "scratch" and would have hidden the bulk of the
# suite.
test_suites/codes/rag_cli.quanta
test_suites/codes/rag_cli_minimal.quanta
# Ad-hoc "compile everything" scratch drivers, not gate tests.
test_suites/codes/test_all_*.quanta
# Numbered scratch iterations left by past debugging (x25519_str_debug2..11,
# x25519_mul_scalar_test2..4, ...). Narrow on purpose: the *_test2/_test3 forms
# also match REAL tracked tests (simd_test2, trait_test2), and
# std_secure_sha3_test_* is a tracked suite, so none of those are ignored here.
test_suites/codes/*_debug[0-9]*.quanta
test_suites/codes/x25519_*_test[0-9].quanta
test_suites/codes/x25519_*_step_test[0-9]*.quanta
test_suites/codes/std_aes_gcm_min.quanta

# --- explicitly ALLOWED ---
!/tools/
!/.github/
!.gitignore
!README.md
!QUANTA.png
!/compiler/
!/docs/
!/lib/
!/tests/
!gap_specs.json
# (test_suites/ contents are un-ignored in the block immediately above this one,
#  together with the re-exclusions for bin/ and the scratch probes.)
!/tools/              # CI needs fuzz + diff_test; same silent-miss trap as test_suites
!/tools/**
!/.github/            # CI workflows must be tracked
!/.github/**
# but exclude tool SCRATCH OUTPUTS (build artifacts), only SOURCE is tracked:
tools/**/out/
tools/**/crashes/
tools/**/*.bin

# Build/fixpoint SCRATCH goes to temp/ in the project root (see line ~34), never
# under compiler/<VER>/. compiler/ holds ONLY src/ + bin/ + STATE.md.
# (debug/ was previously created under compiler/<VER>/debug — that is gone; this
# negation is intentionally NOT present so accidental compiler/**/debug creation
# would surface in `git status` and get caught.)

# --- internal / local-only (never pushed) ---
# The un-anchored names below are intentional for the directories that have NO
# explicit "!" re-inclusion above (systems, agents, bootstrap, scripts, and the
# dot-dirs). A bare `scripts/` matches at ANY depth, so it also swallowed
# test_suites/scripts/ -- and because a later rule beats an earlier negation,
# every NEW CI gate script under test_suites/ was silently dropped while the
# pre-existing ones survived only because they were added before this rule.
# Anchor those to the repo root.
#
# tools/ is deliberately NOT listed here: it already has `!/tools/**` above
# (CI needs fuzz + diff_test), and re-ignoring it here would beat that negation.
/systems/
/agents/
/bootstrap/
/scripts/
/.hyperresearch/
/.claude/
/scratch/
/temp/

# 0.0.220: the `/*` catch-all above would drop these. Both are meant to be
# versioned:
#   config/  -- the single place a path lives. Losing it means every script
#               reverts to its own hardcoded copy, which is the problem the
#               config exists to remove.
#   scripts/rag_*.py + rag_config.py -- the RAG tooling that reads the config.
#               The rest of scripts/ stays ignored; it is scratch and build
#               tooling, not part of the contract.
# `/*` ignores config/ as a directory, and gitignore will not re-include a file
# whose PARENT is excluded. The negation must therefore be on the DIRECTORY, not
# on its contents -- same trap as test_suites/ above. Un-ignore the directory,
# then ignore everything in it except rag.conf, so a stray scratch file dropped
# there does not get committed.
!/config/
/config/*
!/config/rag.conf
!/scripts/
/scripts/*
!/scripts/rag_config.py
!/scripts/build_rag.py
!/scripts/build_rag_sqlite.py
!/scripts/fast_rag.py
!/scripts/rag_cli.py
!/scripts/rag_helper.py
!/scripts/rag_server.py
!/scripts/test_rag.py
!/scripts/test_rag_pipeline.py
!/scripts/rag_embed_file.py
# The finetuning scripts. These name the LFM base models by absolute path, so
# moving the model tree breaks every one of them at once and silently -- the
# scripts still parse, they just fail at load. Versioned so the move is a
# one-place change, like config/rag.conf.
!/scripts/train_lfm25_*.py
!/scripts/continue_lfm25_*.py
# The later quantisation phases, which load the LFM GGUFs. Same reason.
!/scripts/phase3_push.py
!/scripts/phase3_v2.py
!/scripts/phase4_extended.py
!/scripts/phase5_q4.py
!/scripts/cumulative_phase1.py
!/scripts/cumulative_phase2.py

# --- CI gate inputs (under test_suites/, already un-ignored above) ---
# test_suites/ as a whole is un-ignored; nothing else needed here.

# --- compiler golden binaries + self-hosting SOURCE are NEVER ignorable ---
# These two negations guarantee a future broad ignore can never silently drop
# compiler/<VER>/bin (promoted golden seed) or compiler/<VER>/src (source).
# Order matters: they must follow the !/compiler/ negation above.
!compiler/**/bin/
!compiler/**/src/

# --- test_suites/ generated output ---
# Already excluded alongside the re-includes above (test_suites/bin/ and the
# scratch probes); the extra out/ and crashes/ patterns live here because they
# only ever appear in tool output subtrees. LAST match wins, so these hold.

# --- junk ---
vgcore.*
*.core
*.bin
qfio_test.bin
raw.txt
rt.txt
ergz_pass_placeholder

# compiler-specific: keep compiler/<VER>/src/ (SOURCE ONLY) + STATE.md + bin/ tracked.
# src/ must contain SOURCE ONLY — never binaries. bin/ holds the promoted seed
# (rebuilt by CI from src/) and IS tracked. Scratch builds live in temp/ (ignored),
# never under compiler/. STATE.md is the per-version release record — TRACKED.
qc_boot
qc_self
qc_boot_n
qc_self2
qc_a
qc_b
qc055
qc055b
qc_dbg*
*.sym
*.log
s1.log
s2.log
s3.log
learning/

# Scratch cwd for gate test runs (0.0.219): test programs that write
# files must not drop them in the project root.
test_suites/run/

# Upstream-generated GGUF block fixtures. These are COMMITTED DATA, not build
# output: test_read_formats.quanta reads them and reduces them in Quanta to check
# the Q2_K/Q3_K/Q4_1/Q5_0/Q5_1/Q8_K dequantizers against a reference that is not
# this codebase. Regenerating them is a deliberate manual act
# (scripts/audit/gen_fixtures.py), never part of the test command, so they must
# be in the tree or the formats are unverified on a fresh clone.
!/tests/fixtures/*.bin

# The offline fixture generator. One-time use only, calls upstream llama.cpp
# through ctypes. Not on any test or build path -- the production and test paths
# are pure Quanta. Tracked so a fixture can be regenerated and audited, not so
# it can be called at test time.
# `/scripts/*` above prunes subdirectories outright, so no path rule beneath it
# can ever match a file INSIDE scripts/audit/. Un-ignoring just the file does
# nothing (verified with git check-ignore -v). The audit tooling has to be
# re-admitted at the directory level; the allowlist then keeps the rest of
# scripts/ pruned as intended.
!/scripts/audit/
/scripts/audit/*
!/scripts/audit/bisect_test_chain.py
!/scripts/audit/c_oracle.c
!/scripts/audit/dequant_diff.py
!/scripts/audit/dequant_k_expect.py
!/scripts/audit/dequant_oracle.py
!/scripts/audit/f32_conv_check.py
!/scripts/audit/f32_reference.py
!/scripts/audit/gen_fixtures.py
!/scripts/audit/gen_tokenizer_ref.py
!/scripts/audit/gguf_meta_dump.py
!/scripts/audit/gguf_walk_reference.py
!/scripts/audit/lfm2_tok_ref.py
!/scripts/audit/read_formats_oracle.py
!/scripts/audit/run_gguf_tests.py
